> User jacquewedding (283943)
Request Time: 0 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.194.19.164","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":76274,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"30a333c059dba77d5480987b2463d0f6","RawContent":"[quote name=\"WeddingDayStory\" post=\"1915095\" timestamp=\"1469826739\"]\nA note to all brides thinking about doing this on their weddings --- do it! Your photographer will love you.\n \nAlthough we understand that guests and family usually want to take their own pictures and capture memories of their own during the ceremony, it is the one special moment you have all gathered there to share, so it only makes sense to ask your loved ones to be there. In the moment with you.\n \nMake sure to ask your photographer if they can provide you with the service of uploading images to a private, online gallery.\n \nWhat we do is send the couple a link to where the images will be, with the option of having guests sign up to receive an update once the images are posted (which is only 7 to 12 business days after the wedding). That way, everyone can access the ceremony images, share them on Facebook or print them out :) \n \nWe hope the unplugged wedding trend is here to stay!\n \nThis one post that became viral says it very well too: [url=\"http:\/\/www.today.com\/style\/unplugged-weddings-photographers-anti-phone-rant-goes-viral-t55546\"]http:\/\/www.today.com\/style\/unplugged-weddings-photographers-anti-phone-rant-goes-viral-t55546[\/url]\n \n :P[\/quote]This Is Such A Good Idea, Even With My Guest List Only Being 30 It Seems It Would Prove To Be More Beneficial.","Attachments":[],"Id":1915182,"PostDate":1470409121,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>WeddingDayStory, on 29 July 2016 - 05:12 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>A note to all brides thinking about doing this on their weddings --- do it! Your photographer will love you.<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nAlthough we understand that guests and family usually want to take their own pictures and capture memories of their own during the ceremony, it is the one special moment you have all gathered there to share, so it only makes sense to ask your loved ones to be there. In the moment with you.<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nMake sure to ask your photographer if they can provide you with the service of uploading images to a private, online gallery.<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nWhat we do is send the couple a link to where the images will be, with the option of having guests sign up to receive an update once the images are posted (which is only 7 to 12 business days after the wedding). That way, everyone can access the ceremony images, share them on Facebook or print them out <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nWe hope the unplugged wedding trend is here to stay!<br>\n\u00a0<br>\nThis one post that became viral says it very well too:\u00a0<a href='http:\/\/www.today.com\/style\/unplugged-weddings-photographers-anti-phone-rant-goes-viral-t55546' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>http:\/\/www.today.com...es-viral-t55546<\/a><br>\n\u00a0<br>\n <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/tongue.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':P' \/><\/p><\/div><\/div>\n<br>\nThis Is Such A Good Idea, Even With My Guest List Only Being 30 It Seems It Would Prove To Be More Beneficial. \r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><span style=\"color:#ffa07a;\"><span style=\"font-size:18px;\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia, serif;\">#ProjectDreamWedding On A Journey To Our Dream Wedding!\u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\u00a0<\/span><\/span><\/span>","Email":"johnsonspartyof2@gmail.com","IpAddress":"162.239.253.193","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1470347711,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-287511.jpg?_r=1470362394","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Johnsonspartyof2","Id":287511,"Name":"Johnsonspartyof2","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":11,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
